Z||000000||Rrazzz||06-30-2000||06:44 PM||||Per the owner's manual, the Helms service manual, etc. the 1988 4 cylinder should have an oil capacity of 4 quarts. However, my car takes about 4.2 quarts to reach the BOTTOM of the add zone on the dip stick. I've been using 4.7 quarts, which puts it about in the center of the add zone. I think its got the correct dip stick; its stamped #10184924. I don't know how to check if its the correct dip stick tube. Note: this can't be due to long versus short oil filters because the 88 4 cylinder's filter in inside the oil pan.<P>How much oil do other 88 4 cylinders hold?<BR>Does anyone else have this problem?<BR>Any opinions on whether I should fill based on a specific amount/capacity or based on reading on dip stick?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rrazzz||07-01-2000||09:34 PM||||Does anyone that owns a 4 cylinder w/ the oil filter inside the oil pan change their own oil? How much oil does it take to indicate full on the dip stick?||||reg||5
